[h1]Random New World 1.3.0[/h1]

Generate Africa and Oceania alongside or instead of America (with Eurasia planned), plus natural wastelands, river-first geography, compact sea cells, the Terra Incognita window theme, and Proton Experimental support. For EU5 1.4.* (verified on 1.4.9).

[h2]🌍 New features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Optional Africa and Oceania.[/b] Switch America, Africa and Oceania on or off independently in one world and one mod. Each continent has its own world types, quick choices, whole-map sketches and drawable sheet in the land editor. [i]Keep the real Americas[/i] also works alongside generated Africa and Oceania.
[*][b]African starts and land bridges.[/b] Choose four outcomes for Morocco's Iberian holdings and keep the Mamluks or form an independent Sultanate of Damascus; restored Morocco and Mamluks carry over their 1337 pops, towns, markets, institutions and buildings. Configure optional or required land bridges to Asia and an optional [b]Allow a land connection to Iberia (no strait)[/b] that closes the Mediterranean.
[*][b]Natural wastelands.[/b] Impassable locations now include dunes, plateaus, hills and flat wilds (tundra, taiga, jungle) alongside mountains, placed by climate and terrain and named by their ground in all eleven languages.
[*][b]River-first, climate-sized geography.[/b] Coastal cordilleras, seasonal rainfall and drainage run before location partitioning so larger rivers become borders and locations scale with climate, terrain and continent defaults. Raw materials blend small habitat classes with broader ones.
[*][b]Compact sea cells and world sea route.[/b] Open water uses an even rectangular grid with local partitions at shores and narrow straits, and [i]Keep a sea route around the world[/i] opens a narrow passage only where continents leave none.
[*][b]Terra Incognita appearance and classic parity.[/b] Settings → Appearance adds the aged-chart Terra Incognita look in the Tauri window, physical maps render as lit sheets with kept Old World lands, progress shows nine phases, and the classic Qt window matches every feature.
[/list]

[h2]🔧 Fixes and improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Added an [i]icuuc.dll[/i] forwarder so the classic window opens under Valve's Proton Experimental on Linux and Steam Deck.
[*]Kept passable land locations under the game's city-grid stack limit to prevent crashes when opening city details, and scaled population by planned cell area rather than final pixel count.
[*]Fixed marriage/heir law parsing, Australian reform assignment, retained rivers cut at replaced edges, Mediterranean basin naming, open-Atlantic island sites, and machine-wide huge-page stalls during exports.
[*]Faster exact-output generation with native Rust kernels and strip processing.
[/list]

[quote][b]Updating:[/b] Targets EU5 1.4.* (latest verified: 1.4.9, build 26655995); most patches in the 1.4 branch work without a generator update. Generate a new world for epoch 64; keep existing world mods for ongoing saves. Turn on [b]Experimental features[/b] in Settings to make worlds by epochs 63 (1.2.2), 62 (1.2.1) or 61 (1.2.0). Use one RNW world at a time, allow about 8 GB of free RAM, and restart EU5 when switching maps.[/quote]

